FLAKY TESTS BIBLIOGRAPHY - "SHORT" REFERENCES VERSION

Contributors:
- Owain Parry
- Gregory Kapfhammer
- Michael Hilton 
- Phil McMinn

Style guide:
- Use {} as opposed to  ""
- A tab/indent is two spaces
- Surround whole words with curly brackets in titles to preserve captilization, not just first letters
- Order of fields:  
    - Conference paper: author, title, booktitle, year
    - Journal paper: author, title, journal, year
- Key is formed by first author surname, followed by publication year, followed by b/c/d... if multiple publications for that author in that year
- Entries ordered by key

Additional short version guide:
- Only use conference acronyms for "booktitle"
- Omit page numbers, volumes, etc. (see "Order of fields" above)

